# CR-9.1 autonomy step 1: STANDARD-catalog physical self-heal for the fleet +
# skchat adapters. OFF by default: this file ships as an .example and is NOT
# installed. Until it (or SKOPERATOR_HONOR=1) is set, --execute only writes
# signed spec annotations (fleet_act); nothing is physically actuated.
#
# THE ONE-LINE FLIP (Chef, after the gameday + freeze drills pass):
#   cp data/systemd/skoperator.service.d/honor.conf.example \
#      ~/.config/systemd/user/skoperator.service.d/honor.conf
#   systemctl --user daemon-reload
#
# It resets ExecStart and re-adds it with --honor. It applies AFTER execute.conf
# (drop-ins load alphabetically; "honor" > "execute"), so it wins. Atlas then
# physically actuates auto STANDARD-catalog fixes (fleet restart_service, skchat
# restart-daemon / restart-telegram-bridge), each recorded as an ITIL change.
# Majors still park, and freeze always wins.
#
# TO REVERT: rm ~/.config/systemd/user/skoperator.service.d/honor.conf
#            systemctl --user daemon-reload
[Service]
ExecStart=
ExecStart=%h/.skenv/bin/skoperator run --execute --honor
